# Line-ending policy: Windows development host, Linux Docker runtime.
#
# THE KEY CONSTRAINT: the containers do not COPY these files, they BIND-MOUNT
# the working tree (see compose/*/docker-compose.yml -> ./scripts:/usr/local/bin/scripts).
# So the bytes sitting in the Windows working tree are the exact bytes Linux
# executes. A CRLF entrypoint.sh fails in-container with the classic
#   /usr/local/bin/scripts/entrypoint.sh: /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter
# That rules out the usual Windows setup (`eol=crlf` on checkout): we need LF in
# the working tree itself, not just inside the repo.
# Hence: LF everywhere, on checkout as well as in the object store. Git handles
# it; Windows editors (VS Code, modern Notepad) all read and write LF fine.
# The only CRLF exceptions are Windows-native scripts, which never enter a
# container.
# After changing this file, renormalize the existing working tree once:
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git commit -m "Normalize line endings to LF"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: auto-detect text vs binary, and store/check out all text as LF.
# text=auto is deliberate — it protects undeclared binaries (and the UTF-16
# requirements file noted below) from being mangled by normalization.
*                   text=auto eol=lf
# Executed or parsed inside the Linux container — LF is mandatory, not cosmetic.
# Declared explicitly so detection can never get it wrong.
*.sh                text eol=lf
*.py                text eol=lf
*.yaml              text eol=lf
*.yml               text eol=lf
Dockerfile          text eol=lf
*.dockerfile        text eol=lf
.dockerignore       text eol=lf
.env.example        text eol=lf
# Data and docs. Read by Python on both sides; LF keeps diffs honest.
# NOTE: *.txt is intentionally NOT forced to `text` — docker/pyscenedetect/
# requirements-docker.txt is currently UTF-16LE (see REORG_REPAIR_PLAN.md §11).
# Forcing `text` would corrupt it; text=auto detects it as binary and leaves it
# alone. Once that file is regenerated as UTF-8, `*.txt text eol=lf` can be added.
*.json              text eol=lf
*.csv               text eol=lf
*.md                text eol=lf
*.gitattributes     text eol=lf
*.gitignore         text eol=lf
Makefile            text eol=lf
# Windows-native scripts — never mounted into a container, must stay CRLF or
# cmd.exe/PowerShell misbehave.
*.bat               text eol=crlf
*.cmd               text eol=crlf
*.ps1               text eol=crlf
# Binary — never normalize, never diff. Test fixtures live in tests/expected/.
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp3               binary
*.flac              binary
*.wav               binary
*.jpg               binary
*.jpeg              binary
*.png               binary
*.pdf               binary
*.docx              binary
*.zip               binary
*.aup3              binary
*.dat               binary
*.exe               binary
*.dll               binary
*.pyd               binary
*.pyc               binary

*.flac filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.docx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp3 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
